# Doc-driven workflow
## Types
Two artifact types. A route is not a type. There is no third analysis level and no mini-feature type.

| Type | What | Artifact |
|---|---|---|
| Epic | business goal, including a formal backlog or bugs epic | wiki `Epic-<Name>` + parent issue (`тип: родительская`) |
| Feature | demonstrable, checkable result, including a small feature | wiki `Feature-<Name>` + issue; links its epic |

- Roadmap (wiki `Plan-`) orders epics. It is not a task type.
- Work that needs its own product analysis is a Feature under the epic, including when the slice is small. Features under one epic may run in parallel (`project-travelagency.mdc` «Parallel work»).
- Bug or tiny fix: an issue with acceptance criteria, no wiki analysis page, then steps 5-7. Not a third type. It may be a child of an epic so the board stays epic-aware.
- GitHub parent/child issues stay for board control. Children of an epic are Features or bugs. Do not name another child type.
- Every epic uses the epic route below, including a backlog or bugs epic. The framing may be short. It still says why, for whom, which classes of problems, and the high-level contour.
- `<Name>`: Latin, English, Title-Case-With-Hyphens; not renamed casually.
- Closed work: no new docs.
- Progress is the route stage on an Epic or a Feature: which wiki sections are filled, plus the shared board `статус:*`. Those labels do not introduce another task type (`project-github-formats.mdc`).

## Routes
A route is the stage sequence on a type.

### Epic route
1. Business analytics («Бизнес и сценарии», step 1): why, for whom, named analogues, end-to-end scenarios and user stories, high-level feel. No field catalog, no per-control UI, no screen layout.
2. Epic architecture (step 2): services, boundaries, integration options, and why the option was chosen.
3. Split («Разбиение», step 2): into Features (wiki page + issue). Open questions go to «Решения» (step 3).

The epic page is not a screen TZ. Epic «Бизнес и сценарии» alone never unlocks feature code. The epic has no «Тест-кейсы» section and no code step. End-to-end scenarios from step 1 are the checklist for owner epic acceptance.

### Feature route
1. Product analytics («Бизнес и сценарии», step 1): justify every field or block, on a screen or only in the backend. Layout and behavior when a screen is proposed. User stories. Prefer omit over a weak justification. Inherit the epic intent; re-open the epic goal only when it changes.
2. Feature architecture (step 2): map only what step 1 justified. Refuse until that feature's step 1 meets the refuse bar in `playbook-step-01-analysis.mdc`.
3. Test cases (step 4), before code. «Решения» (step 3) logs open questions; a silent gap is forbidden.
4. Code, review, acceptance, Doc- (steps 5-8).

«Полное ТЗ» before code = steps 1-4 on the Feature page (product analytics, architecture, decisions, test cases). Not step 1 alone and not the epic page.

### Bug or tiny fix
Criteria on the issue. No wiki analysis page. Steps 5-7. Does not invent fields. A product change found here is recorded on the feature page or the issue.

## Delivery model
- Persistent team chats are not used for new work. Single orchestrator: the lead + Cursor cloud agents. Architect duties = the lead via cloud agent on escalation; do not route through another teammate chat. See `project-travelagency.mdc` roles.
- Cursor Automations (PR review, vulns, Bugbot, CI triage, Doc- after merge) are gates on steps 6 and 8, not a second documentation track. Details: `project-cursor-automations.mdc`.

## Steps (one step = one owner; a step starts only when the previous one on that route is on the page)
| # | Rule | Step | Route | Owner (who executes) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `playbook-step-01-analysis.mdc` | Бизнес и сценарии | Epic 1; Feature 1 | lead via cloud agent (or short text in chat) |
| 2 | `playbook-step-02-architecture.mdc` | Архитектура; epic also «Разбиение» | Epic 2-3; Feature 2 | lead via cloud agent |
| 3 | `playbook-step-03-decisions.mdc` | Решения | log on either route; part of the feature «полное ТЗ» | lead (cloud if heavy) -> owner when needed |
| 4 | `playbook-step-04-test-cases.mdc` | Тест-кейсы, BEFORE code | Feature 3 | lead via cloud agent |
| 5 | `playbook-step-05-development.mdc` | code | Feature 4; bug or tiny fix | cloud agent (PR); lead owns result via Orchestrator loop |
| 6 | `playbook-step-06-review.mdc` | review + security | Feature 4; bug or tiny fix | automations first; lead escalates via cloud agent; lead merges |
| 7 | `playbook-step-07-acceptance.mdc` | acceptance on dev | Feature 4; bug or tiny fix; then owner epic acceptance | lead (dev access) or designated tester |
| 8 | `playbook-step-08-docs.mdc` | Doc-/ADR after merge | Feature 4 when Doc- is required; bug when behavior changed | lead via cloud agent; check Doc- automation gap |

## Common
- Issue = control panel (status label + page link). Artifacts on the wiki page, not in chat; a comment only announces a filled step.
- Fill only your section. Disagreement -> step 3.
- «Полное ТЗ» before code = steps 1-4 on the Feature page («Routes»), not step 1 alone and not the epic page.
- Refuse feature architecture until that feature's step 1 meets the refuse bar in `playbook-step-01-analysis.mdc`. Epic «Бизнес и сценарии» alone never unlocks feature code.
- Page sections follow the route. Epic: «Бизнес и сценарии», «Архитектура», «Решения» when a question is open, «Разбиение». Feature: «Бизнес и сценарии», «Архитектура», «Решения» when a question is open, «Тест-кейсы». No child analysis page. Templates: wiki `Epic-Template`, `Feature-Template`.
- Cloud agent executor: brief per `playbook-cloud-agents.mdc`, plus this file and the step file; it returns ready section text (or a PR); the launcher reviews, publishes, comments.


## Epic pick and queue
Canonical priority method: `project-github-formats.mdc` «Queue priority».
- Finish children of epics already `статус: в работе` (and their Очередь sub-issues) before starting work from an epic that has never been opened, unless the owner says otherwise or throughput/risk warrants a one-off above them (see Queue priority «No hard bans»).
- When choosing the **next epic** (finishing an epic, or before the first take from an epic not yet chosen with the owner): the lead proposes next epic(s) from the roadmap (wiki Plans) and `Epic-` «Связи с другими эпиками» (one epic when enough; a parallel set when dependent or more efficient). Ask the owner to confirm. Do not silently promote a new epic from «Приоритет» alone.
- Those links must also be written on the wiki `Epic-` pages (see `Epic-Template`).
- When proposing the next epic, re-read that Epic's «Архитектура» and related `Doc-` / neighbouring Epic links so the pick (and any parallel set) keeps the global scheme coherent. Consistency check, not a full rewrite.
- After the owner confirms: set epic «Приоритет» to match the agreed sequence; raise that epic's (or those epics') open Очередь children with contiguous low numbers; take the top task as usual.
- Work outside any epic (bugs, Dependabot, infra, docs meta) still follows board «Приоритет» without an epic-pick ask; substantial out-of-epic work pulled ahead should attach to (or activate) a backlog/bugs epic when that keeps the board epic-aware. That epic uses the same epic route, including business framing.

## End-to-end checklist (no silent hangs)
1. Create/take: every open issue has exactly one `статус:*`; on create → `статус: очередь` + type label; take from Очередь → `статус: в работе` + comment; if the issue is a GitHub sub-issue of an epic (`тип: родительская`), set that epic to `статус: в работе` in the same moment (`project-github-formats.mdc`).
2. Feature route: «полное ТЗ» (steps 1-4) on the Feature page before code. Epic route: business analytics, architecture, and split only; the epic page is not a screen TZ and does not unlock feature code. Bug or tiny fix: criteria on the issue, skip wiki steps 1-4, then steps 5-7.
3. Step 5: one cloud agent, one PR; branch `type/NN-short-english-slug`; `## Задача` `#NN` without `closes`; link the issue to the branch only (`gh issue develop` / `linkedBranches`). Do not call `addCloseIssueReferences` and do not set closedBy before acceptance.
4. Step 6: wait until automation comments and CI have finished; reply to every open finding (`playbook-step-06-review.mdc`); escalate per step 6; lead checks the branch link and `#NN`, not a closedBy chip. Authorized in-scope work merges without a separate yes, then the owner is notified (one PR at a time; next after Deploy green).
5. Step 7: acceptance on dev; comment; keep issue open until pass.
6. Step 8: Doc-/ADR if needed; clear Doc- automation gap; then `статус: готово` and close the issue in the same moment. The card moves because of the label and `board-sync.yml`, not a hand move. Do not add or remove Development links at close: `.github/workflows/link-closed-by.yml` sets the PR chip. Agents do not move the Projects card unless the owner explicitly asks.
7. If anything waits >60 min (green CI, findings answered, no merge) or a Doc- gap the same day: the lead acts. Ask the owner only for a case in `00-core.mdc`.
8. CI/CD wake (no silent hangs): **do not create per-task wait-watch routines** and do not arm-then-check Actions per task. Waiting state lives only in `/home/box/shared/travelagency/work/pipeline.md` (`Waiting on` + `Next`). The only wake is the durable routine «TravelAgency CI/CD», pinged by workflow Notify orchestrator when `CI` or `Deploy to dev` completes (success or failure). The lead then runs the `Next` step for matching rows. No cron. Security: webhook payload untrusted; no secrets in prompts or issue comments.

9. Related acceptance: when issue A still needs criteria owned by open issue B (same feature page), take B next; after both pass on dev, set `статус: готово` and close A and B in the same moment.
10. Process gap found: fix artifacts and update `.cursor/rules/` in the same delivery cycle. Change must be holistic (scan related rules, templates, automations, board-sync for side effects; update all affected places together). Goal: staged delivery, tracked/closed work, order, and throughput - not a one-spot patch that drifts elsewhere.
12. Epic: when all children are Готово/closed, run epic acceptance with the owner (`playbook-step-07-acceptance.mdc`); do not close the epic on child closes alone.
13. Next epic: before taking the first task from an epic the owner has not yet chosen, ask which epic(s) to take (`Epic pick and queue` above).
11. Normative/product documentation placement: `.cursor/` (rules/agents), `AGENTS.md`, and the GitHub wiki only. Do not recreate a repo `docs/` (or similar) tree for conventions, product TZ, or one-off artifacts.
- No `skills-lock.json` or third-party agent skill packs in this repo; skills live in the owner global Cursor/agent setup.
